# Frontend code formatting and style

## EditorConfig rules

- **Indent**: 2 spaces for all files
- **Quotes**: single quotes for TypeScript/JavaScript (`'string'`)
- **End of file**: always add a blank line at end of file (`insert_final_newline = true`)
- **Trailing whitespace**: remove trailing spaces (`trim_trailing_whitespace = true`)

## Whitespace in objects

- **After colon**: `{ a: 1 }` (space after `:`)
- **After comma**: `{ a: 1, b: 2 }` (space after `,`)
- **Inside braces**: `{ a: 1 }` (spaces inside `{}`)
- **Around arrow**: `() => {}` (spaces around `=>`)

Example:
```typescript
// ✅ Correct
const obj = { a: 1, b: 2 };
const arr = [{ id: 'any', name: 'All locations' }];
const fn = (x: number) => x * 2;

// ❌ Incorrect
const obj = {a:1,b:2};
const arr = [{ id:'any', name:'All locations' }];
const fn = (x:number)=>x*2;
```

**Important**: Always use spaces after colons in objects and object arrays, including constant arrays and exported data.

## Angular decorators

- **Spaces after colon** - all decorator properties must have spaces after the colon
- **Spaces in arrays** - spaces after the opening bracket and before the closing bracket in `imports`, `styleUrls`

Example:
```typescript
// ✅ Correct
@Component({
  selector: 'app-oil',
  standalone: true,
  templateUrl: './oil.component.html',  // REQUIRED
  styleUrls: [ './oil.component.scss' ], // REQUIRED
  imports: [
    CommonModule,
    FormsModule,
  ],
})

// ❌ Incorrect - missing templateUrl
@Component({
  selector: 'app-oil',
  standalone: true,
  // templateUrl missing - ERROR
  styleUrls: [ './oil.component.scss' ],
  imports: [ CommonModule ],
})

// ❌ Incorrect - missing styleUrls
@Component({
  selector: 'app-oil',
  standalone: true,
  templateUrl: './oil.component.html',
  // styleUrls missing - ERROR
  imports: [ CommonModule ],
})

// ❌ Incorrect - formatting
@Component({
  selector:'app-oil',
  standalone:true,
  templateUrl:'./oil.component.html',
  styleUrls:[ './oil.component.scss' ],
  imports:[
    CommonModule,
    FormsModule,
  ],
})
```

**Important**:
- Always use spaces after colons in decorators (`@Component`, `@Pipe`, `@Directive`, `@Injectable`, etc.) and spaces inside arrays (`[ ... ]`)
- **All components MUST contain template/templateUrl and styles/styleUrls**

## Access modifiers

- **Always explicit** - always specify access modifiers (`private`, `protected`, `public`)
- **`private readonly`** - for all injected services in the constructor
- **`protected`** - for methods and properties used in templates
- **`readonly`** - for constant properties

Example:
```typescript
export class Component {
  private readonly service: SomeService;  // ✅
  protected readonly resource = 'path';   // ✅
  public title: string;                   // ✅
  // someProperty: string;                // ❌ No modifier
}
```

## Naming

- **Components**: PascalCase with `Component` suffix (`VacancyComponent`)
- **Services**: PascalCase with `Service` suffix (`TranslationService`)
- **Interfaces**: PascalCase (`Vacancy`, `ResumeSection`)
- **Types**: PascalCase with `Id` or `Type` suffix (`LocationId`)
- **Constants**: camelCase (`vacanciesRoutes`, `vacancies`)
- **Methods**: camelCase (`onSubmit()`, `getVacancyById()`)
- **Properties**: camelCase (`isResourceLoaded`, `vacancy`)

## Imports

- **Required sort order**: imports must be sorted in the following order:
  1. `@angular/*` - all Angular imports (at the top)
  2. External libraries - all imports from external npm packages (jose, jwt-decode, rxjs, luxon, etc.)
  3. `@workspace/*` - all imports from internal workspace libraries (near the bottom, but not at the very bottom)
  4. Relative imports `from '.'` - all local imports with relative paths (at the very bottom)
- **Consolidate imports**: all imports from the same module must be merged into one import
- **Blank lines**: separate groups with blank lines only when it improves readability
- **Sort within group**: imports within each group must be sorted alphabetically

Example:
```typescript
// ✅ Correct - consolidated imports
import { Component, DestroyRef, ViewChild } from '@angular/core';
import { takeUntilDestroyed } from '@angular/core/rxjs-interop';
import { FormBuilder, FormGroup, ReactiveFormsModule, Validators } from '@angular/forms';
import { Router, RouterLink } from '@angular/router';
import { JWTPayload } from 'jose';
import { jwtDecode } from 'jwt-decode';
import { Observable, tap, catchError, throwError, map, of, switchMap, take } from 'rxjs';
import { finalize } from 'rxjs/operators';
import { ROUTE_PATH, RouterPaths } from '@workspace/core';
import { ApiResponse, AuthTokenService, TokenModel, ApiService, TimeSpan, UUID } from '@workspace/shared';
import { LanguageSelectorComponent, RequestStatusComponent, RequestStatusStore } from '@workspace/ui';
import { AUTH_CONFIG, AuthConfig } from './auth-config';
import { AuthService } from './auth.service';
import { AuthStore } from './auth.store';

// ❌ Incorrect - wrong order
import { AuthService } from './auth.service';
import { Component } from '@angular/core';
import { ROUTE_PATH } from '@workspace/core';
import { Observable } from 'rxjs';

// ❌ Incorrect - non-consolidated imports from the same module
import { Component } from '@angular/core';
import { DestroyRef } from '@angular/core';
import { ViewChild } from '@angular/core';
import { Router } from '@angular/router';
import { RouterLink } from '@angular/router';
import { ROUTE_PATH } from '@workspace/core';
import { RouterPaths } from '@workspace/core';

// ✅ Correct - consolidated imports
import { Component, DestroyRef, ViewChild } from '@angular/core';
import { Router, RouterLink } from '@angular/router';
import { ROUTE_PATH, RouterPaths } from '@workspace/core';
```

**Important**: Always sort imports in the specified order. Relative imports (`from '.'`) must be at the bottom of the import list.

## Comments

- **In English** - all comments must be in English
- **Explain "why"** - comments should explain the reason, not describe the obvious
- **Brevity** - comments should be brief and to the point

Example:
```typescript
// ❌ Bad
// Get ID from route
const id = this.route.snapshot.paramMap.get('id');

// ✅ Good
// Get ID from route to look up vacancy in the array
const vacancyId = this.route.snapshot.paramMap.get('id');
```

## File structure

- **One class/interface per file** - each file should contain one primary export
- **File name = class name** - file name should match the class name (kebab-case)
- **index.ts for re-export** - use `index.ts` for re-export from directories
